subQuestions.answerMdx:
Wrap the handler in `useCallback` so its identity only changes when its dependencies do, and wrap the derived list in `useMemo`:

```jsx
const onSelect = useCallback((id) => addToCart(id), [addToCart])
const visible = useMemo(
  () => items.filter((i) => i.name.includes(query)).sort((a, b) => a.price - b.price),
  [items, query],
)
```

Now `onSelect` keeps the same reference between renders while its deps are unchanged, so `React.memo`'s shallow compare passes and the row is skipped; `visible` is recomputed only when `items` or `query` actually change. Dependencies must list every value the callbacks read, or React will cache a stale version.

subQuestions.answerMdxZh:
用 `useCallback` 包裹处理器，让它的引用只在依赖变化时才改变；再用 `useMemo` 包裹派生列表：

```jsx
const onSelect = useCallback((id) => addToCart(id), [addToCart])
const visible = useMemo(
  () => items.filter((i) => i.name.includes(query)).sort((a, b) => a.price - b.price),
  [items, query],
)
```

这样在依赖不变时，`onSelect` 在多次渲染之间保持同一引用，`React.memo` 的浅比较通过，该行被跳过；`visible` 只在 `items` 或 `query` 真正变化时才重算。依赖数组必须列出回调读取到的每个值，否则 React 会缓存一份过期的结果。

